KG42.register("clusters-1c79a0bdb27cb372398c813b",{"id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v142-d-CL002","paper":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization","label":"DSO request reception based on the approved baseline and SESP minimum-cost configuration","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"DSO request reception based on the approved baseline and SESP minimum-cost configuration","market_meaning":"The DSO gives a time-differentiated flexibility request relative to the baseline, and the SESP selects a configuration plan under the approved baseline, established contracts, and resource constraints, and when feasible satisfies the net regulation requirement in the corresponding direction. The priority and direct-control authority under the yellow state limit the coordination and configuration activities.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The three chains belong to the same SESP local flexibility mechanism and respectively provide request definition, configuration decision, and coordination conditions. Upward and downward regulation requests apply under separate conditions; authority under the yellow state does not extend to the red state. R003's daily execution and end-of-period battery restoration conditions retain the case scope; for periods with zero request, zero deviation is not additionally presumed, and when resources are insufficient, the existence of an automatic remedy is likewise not presumed.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The requested quantity and the approved baseline directly determine the configuration constraints, and the coordination chain specifies the recipient, responsibility, and control authority, constituting the same decision unit across submission, coordination, and configuration stages. The payment obligation has independent trigger conditions, and another cluster references the configuration result through an interface. The frozen configuration chain still has mathematical closure and upstream coverage gaps.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Provide the sign, direction, and unit definitions of the DSO request required for configuration."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Undertake resource selection, the cost objective, and the request-satisfaction and device-feasibility constraints."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplement the SESP's reception of requests, baseline approval, priority under the yellow state, and direct-control authority, limiting the responsibility and conditions of configuration activities."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_dso_request","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev33","v141-b-g02-ev34","v141-b-g02-ev35","v141-b-g02-ev36","v141-b-g04-e01"],"rationale":"The request definition and the configuration constraints use the DSO request of the same mechanism, same time period, and same baseline basis; positive and negative directions enter their corresponding constraints respectively, and reverse resource contributions are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g02-ev33"],"rationale":"What the SESP receives is precisely the DSO flexibility request relative to the baseline; this input is not equivalent to obtaining grid-state information, nor does it add request parameters in R004."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-004","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g01-ev-014"],"rationale":"Under the yellow state, the DSO priority and SESP direct-control authority connect with resource selection. The coordination responsibility and the configuration priority condition retain different roles, and the two constraints are not judged to be completely duplicate because of shared evidence."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_f_gr","v141-c-R003::theta::par_f_gd","v141-c-R003::theta::par_w_cd","v141-c-R003::theta::par_w_sp","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-011","v141-b-g02-ev08","v141-b-g02-ev11","v141-b-g02-ev34","v141-b-g02-ev36"],"rationale":"The original text places each asset forecast used as a baseline under the DSO approval condition; the generation and load forecasts in the configuration perform this baseline role. Here only the approval condition and existing inputs are associated, and no approval process or measurement formula is fabricated."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g01-ev-006","v141-b-g02-ev33"],"rationale":"All three places are the frozen bidding.demand node, carrying the definition, configuration input, and reception relationship of the same DSO request; the representative selection is for display only, and the original node references and all chain edges are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g01-ev-014"],"rationale":"Both places refer to the SESP coordinator of this mechanism; unified display does not merge its configuration, priority, or control-authority constraints."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P001","v141-c-R003::theta::par_dso_request"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev33","v141-b-g04-e01"],"rationale":"The definitions, time-period indices, units, and meaning relative to the forecast baseline are consistent, supporting the same requested-quantity interface; the local roles of submission parameter and configuration input are retained separately."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"The request, coordination, and mathematical evidence all remain unverified; this experiment did not perform a B source audit, C2 independent review, or Agent E.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-011","v141-b-g02-ev01","v141-b-g02-ev33","v141-b-g04-e01"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manual review shall check the sources, formulas, and assembly mappings referenced by this cluster; keep candidate status distinct from scientific acceptance."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"B lists Eq. (8) and Eq. (9), but the R003 constraint catalog does not take up these two mutually exclusive CD-state conditions, and continuity and operating time limits alone are insufficient to replace them. The initial-period state of continuity and the index handling for Eq. (12) and Eq. (13) beyond the end of the planning horizon are also not specified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_delta_start","v141-c-R003::x::var_delta_run","v141-c-R003::x::var_delta_end","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C013","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C014"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev18","v141-b-g02-ev19","v141-b-g02-ev20","v141-b-g02-ev22","v141-b-g02-ev23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream shall verify and, in a subsequent C version, take up the omitted conditions and specify the initial state and temporal boundaries; D does not add constraints to the frozen chain."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The battery charge/discharge quantity and SOC only list upper bounds and do not explicitly list nonnegative lower bounds or the recursive initial-period state parameter. The appendix contains a battery discharge indicator variable, but the existing C has no corresponding object or associated constraint, so it cannot be presumed that charge/discharge mutual exclusion has been implemented; end-of-period energy restoration is only a procedural condition in the case.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_sigma_in","v141-c-R003::x::var_sigma_out","v141-c-R003::x::var_sigma_soc","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C012","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C017"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev13","v141-b-g02-ev14","v141-b-g02-ev15","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g04-e06"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the variable domains, initial conditions, and whether a charge/discharge exclusivity mechanism exists in the source model, and distinguish the general model from case terminal conditions; missing formulas must not be supplied based on physical common sense."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G04","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The SP constraints do not yet specify variables outside the window, cross-window overlap, or index boundaries. Eq. (15) aligns the baseline according to T_{k,c}^{start}, while the fee uses V_{k,c}^{start}; how to preserve the meaning of the actual start time when the two differ still needs explanation. Eq. (14) also does not explicitly guarantee that the selected time is not earlier than the baseline start, so it cannot be directly claimed that only postponement occurs or that delay fees are necessarily nonnegative.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C016","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::x::var_gamma","v141-c-R003::x::var_omega","v141-c-R003::x::var_rho","v141-c-R003::theta::par_t_start","v141-c-R003::theta::par_v_start"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev25","v141-b-g02-ev26","v141-b-g02-ev29","v141-b-g02-ev30","v141-b-g02-ev31"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream shall verify the time indices, out-of-window values, compatibility conditions among different windows, and the applicable assumption of postponement only, retaining the current formulas without rearranging them independently."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G05","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The configuration chain takes established contracts as input, but the available time periods are mainly carried by C009 text, and supplier pricing upper limits and contract updates have not formed corresponding C chains. When resources are insufficient to satisfy the request, the existing chains also do not give a shortage-handling rule, and a feasible case cannot be generalized into necessarily satisfying the request.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C009","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-005","v141-b-g01-ev-007","v141-b-g01-ev-008","v141-b-g03-E13"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-flexibility-contract","proposal:v141-b-g01-contract-flexibility-price","v141-b-g02-prop02"],"required_work":"Specify the boundary of external contract inputs and verify the mathematical uptake of available time periods; if extending to contract formation or shortage handling, upstream shall separately provide sourced rules and must not fabricate price upper limits or shortage penalties."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G06","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The dedicated proposals for the flexibility product, DSO request, SESP cost objective, and direct control signal have all not been approved. The existing node bindings cannot reinterpret this service as ordinary energy trading, social welfare maximization, or price-signal coordination.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g01-ev-014","v141-b-g02-ev04","v141-b-g02-ev05"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-flexibility-product","proposal:v141-b-g01-dso-flexibility-request","v141-b-g02-prop01","v141-b-g02-prop03","v141-b-g03-P02"],"required_work":"Manual review shall evaluate the pending proposals and the semantic carrying scope of existing nodes; maintain the current C graph and do not replace ontology approval with a D assembly decision."}]},"rule_refs":["21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R002","21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R003","21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R004"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-464efdadf92efbd8","COMP-62155e4e7998a74f","COMP-c6ecf48e92525ee2"]});
